+paper:
+
+  Dou_nature_2017:
+    cite: "Dou Z, Ghosh K, Vizioli MG, Zhu J, Sen P, Wangensteen KJ, et al. Cytoplasmic chromatin triggers inflammation in senescence and cancer. Nature. 2017;550:402-406."
+    url: "https://doi.org/10.1038/nature24050"
+    summary: "Lamin B1 loss during senescence allows cytoplasmic chromatin fragments (CCF) to form and recruit CGAS, which produces cGAMP (LC-MS-confirmed) and activates STING1, driving RELA/NF-kB-mediated SASP. The axis is required in vivo for immunosurveillance and tumour suppression, and is biased toward NF-kB rather than type-I IFN because p38_MAPK and IL1A suppress IFNB1. The same axis runs chronically in OIS-evaded and cancer cells and correlates with SASP gene expression across CCLE and TCGA; the cytosolic DNA sensor CGAS, not IFI16, drives the response."
+    nucleic_acid_sensors:
+      - CGAS
+      - STING1
+      - IFI16
+      - MAVS
+    genes:
+      - CGAS
+      - STING1
